:c9k5WTmAUygefi6B a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:attribute :BAR5WTmAUygefi66 ;
    ontouml:description """Scope: definition of Multiple Birth Component, its relation to Multiple Birth, and ordering.

Multiple Birth Component is a Single Birth event that represents the delivery of one offspring as part of a Multiple Birth. Each Multiple Birth has two or more components (2..*), and each component belongs to exactly one Multiple Birth (1).

birth position (int, derived, multiplicity 1) records the ordinal delivery position of the component within its Multiple Birth (e.g., 1 = first delivered, 2 = second, ...), derived from the ordering of components (or from recorded clinical sequence).""" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
    ontouml:isPowertype false ;
    ontouml:name "Multiple Birth Component"@en ;
    ontouml:order "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
